bssidx - BSSID Location Lookup Tool

A simple command line tool for looking up WiFi access point locations using Apple's location services. Give it a BSSID (MAC address) and it tells you where that access point is located geographically.

INSTALL

    go install github.com/gnomegl/bssidx@latest

USAGE

    bssidx [flags] BSSID

FLAGS

    -m, -map    Open location in Google Maps
    -a, -all    Show all results instead of exact match only

EXAMPLES

    bssidx aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff
    bssidx -m 00:11:22:33:44:55
    bssidx -a aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff

The tool queries Apple's WiFi location database which contains millions of access points worldwide. Apple collects this data from iOS devices to provide location services.

BUILDING

Requires protoc compiler for the protobuf definitions:

    go generate
    go build

The tool constructs a binary protobuf payload mimicking locationd requests and parses the response to extract latitude/longitude coordinates.
